    "extraction_notes": [
      "Datasheet SHA-256 verified as 2d3eab35c4d2aa913206e8090999c8efb771e0bd9313c563546701a075ba0c91.",
      "Figures 1 and 2 were digitized from the supplied plotted traces at Ta = 25 degC and Ta = 100 degC; plotted reverse-current values are represented as positive magnitudes. No intermediate points were synthesized.",
      "Figure 3 was digitized from the typical junction-capacitance trace at Ta = 25 degC and f = 1 MHz. The electrical-characteristics table separately gives maximum CT = 120 pF at VR = 4 V and f = 1 MHz.",
      "Figure 4 is a thermal power-derating characteristic, included separately from the diode electrical curves; its plotted vertices are PD = 250 mW through Ta = 25 degC and PD = 0 mW at Ta = 125 degC.",
      "Absolute-rating bounds from p. 1 at Ta = 25 degC are VRRM = 60 V, VRMS = 42 V, VDC = 60 V, IF(AV) = 1.0 A, IFSM = 10 A at t = 8.3 ms half-sine wave, PD = 250 mW, Tj = -55 to +150 degC, TSTG = -55 to +150 degC, and RthetaJ-A = 400 degC/W.",
      "The datasheet publishes no reverse-recovery-time, breakdown-voltage, or breakdown-current specification; VRRM and VDC ratings are limits, not breakdown data."
